@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy</PageTitle>

<div class="settings-shell">
    <section class="card-surface settings-card">
        <p class="section-label">Privacy</p>
        <h1>Data handling</h1>
        <p class="panel-copy">
            By default, Habitica credentials stay in this browser and are sent only to Habitica. Optional ChatGPT linking or cloud workspace access requires separate consent to encrypted credential storage on the Companion integration server. Exports, private device sync, and shared party sync do not include your API token.
        </p>

        <div class="settings-grid">
            <MudPaper Class="card-surface action-card" Elevation="0">
                <h2>Optional cloud workspace</h2>
                <p>Cloud task storage requires its own explicit consent, independently of ChatGPT. The workspace server can read task names, notes, categories, projects, goals, completion history and commands. Enabling it also requires encrypted credential storage on the integration server. Private device sync retains its separate encrypted boundary.</p>
                <p>Workspace task and command history remains until explicit workspace deletion. Disconnect revokes workspace sessions and pauses background execution while retaining that history. Delete cloud workspace removes cloud tasks and command history; it does not delete local browser copies, integration credentials, or Habitica records. Delete integration profile separately removes stored credentials. Background execution requires separate opt-in. Local workspace backups are readable and contain no credentials.</p>
            </MudPaper>
            <MudPaper Class="card-surface action-card" Elevation="0">
                <h2>Optional ChatGPT linking</h2>
                <p>When linking is available, Settings asks for explicit consent before sending credentials to the Companion integration server. ChatGPT receives a separate OAuth grant; it never receives the Habitica API token. Disconnect removes stored credentials and denies integration access. Delete integration profile removes the profile record. Browser snapshots, Habitica data and ChatGPT conversations are separate.</p>
                <p>Linking codes expire within ten minutes. Operational audit metadata is limited to thirty days and excludes task text, credentials and conversation text. Hosting logs and backups have separate retention. Management credentials stay in the current tab and are excluded from exports and sync. Losing the management credential requires Habitica revalidation.</p>
            </MudPaper>
            <MudPaper Class="card-surface action-card" Elevation="0">
                <h2>If the app looks out of date</h2>
                <p>Clear this site's browser data and refresh once. This removes old browser files from earlier deployments.</p>
            </MudPaper>

            <MudPaper Class="card-surface action-card" Elevation="0">
                <h2>Habitica credentials</h2>
                <p>Credentials are used to load your Habitica data and protect private device sync. They are not included in exports. Party sync uses a local party claim, so the API token is not sent to Cloudflare party-sync endpoints.</p>
            </MudPaper>

            <MudPaper Class="card-surface action-card" Elevation="0">
                <h2>Local and exported data</h2>
                <p>Saved Habitica data, party history, app messages, gear information, and equipment presets are stored in browser storage. Downloaded backup files are readable, so keep them private.</p>
            </MudPaper>

            <MudPaper Class="card-surface action-card" Elevation="0">
                <h2>Private sync</h2>
                <p>Private device sync stores encrypted data. Shared party sync stores party CRON history, derived party state, roles, settings, and kick records. Local party claims are token-private but trust-based. Hosting providers may process request details such as IP address and timestamps for security.</p>
            </MudPaper>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
